;; hsi's AOT level's classes (bin/hsi check --aot, HE8; doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md): the non-passes of test/haskell/check-hsi-aot.edn, in goi's format. The compiled level keeps eval's one class where it matches (:async-revert: the compiled run equals hsi's, :vs-hsi :same, so GHC's difference is the interpreter's, carried over). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :async-revert
  :title "an interrupted thunk evaluated again from its start"
  :kind :design
  :why "an asynchronous exception interrupting a thunk's evaluation: GHC freezes the evaluation on the stack (raiseAsync's AP_STACK) and the next demand resumes it, hsi reverts the thunk to unevaluated and the next demand starts it again (survey §6.5): the same values, but an unsafePerformIO side effect inside runs twice (samples/AsyncRerun: GHC 1, hsi 2)"
  :decided "review 189's known divergence, classed (HE4e); freezing as GHC's a later choice (HES56, proposed)"
  :results [:fail]
  :ids ["samples/AsyncRerun"]}
 {:id :threaded-way
  :title "a threaded-only test whose normal-way reference is the non-threaded RTS's refusal: hsi's match of it is no verdict"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "all.T runs the test only in the threaded ways; record-ref builds it the one normal way, where GHC's non-threaded RTS refuses or diverges (T21651 and ffi014: status 1, an uncaught IOException; hs_try_putmvar003: its C's \"This test requires -threaded\"; numsparks001: another output than the shipped one), so the recorded run is not the test's own verdict (test/haskell/threaded-way.tsv, bin/hsi own-verdicts). hsi matches that refusal, which is no evidence of the test's behaviour: bin/hsi check records the match :threaded-way (:would :pass), not a pass"
  :decided "HES87 (a), the user 2026-11-08: out of the passes until HES84 (a) (the threaded ways' references, -threaded, and hs_exit's shutdown), which judges them in their own way"
  :results [:threaded-way]
  :ids ["testsuite/ffi/should_run/ffi014"]}
]
